{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation note — the recorded \"28 -> 30\" corpus numbers are stale, and the test asserts the\ndelta instead.\n\nMeasured on `origin/main` (aaf71639b8) with the repo venv, `provider_parity.select_corpus(\neligible_cases())`:\n\n- BEFORE (container cases payload-less): 128 eligible, **26** in the selected corpus\n- AFTER  (all 12 cases carry `children`): 140 eligible, **28** in the selected corpus\n\nThe +12 eligible / +2 selected delta is exactly what the ticket predicted; only the absolute\ntotals differ, because the spec set has changed since story 0d76 recorded 28/30. The container\nspec contributes exactly 2 because `select_corpus` takes the FIRST gold-block and FIRST\ngold-advisory case per spec — and those two are precisely `G3-R-uncovered-ac-rebar` and\n`G3-FP-covered-by-named-consumer-rebar`, the two cases 0d76 measured raising on both arms at\nevery epoch.\n\nSo the new test in `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` asserts\n`len(select_corpus(eligible)) == len(select_corpus(eligible_without_container)) + 2` plus\n`sorted(labels) == [\"advisory\", \"block\"]`, rather than a hard-coded total that would break the\nnext time an unrelated eval spec is added. The description's AC line naming \"30\" should be read\nas that +2 delta.\n\nOn the decision the original AC asked for: I did NOT re-open it. The project's own record\nsettles it — `eval_solver._run_criterion_case` states in its own comment that \"a container\ncriterion with no `children` payload is a fixture error, not a silent pass\", and\n`plan-review-decomp-shape.eval.yaml` is the same kind of spec shipping the payload, with the\nshape documented in its header. Adding payloads is following that record, not choosing between\nopen options. Every `children` list is transcribed from the case's existing `input` prose, so no\n`input`, `expect`, `criterion`, `mode`, `note` or `gold_set` line changed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786098717210149001,"uuid":"a4c16e63-68fe-4e77-bd94-f59b8a3d6c15"}